// keymap.js -- KeyboardEvent.code -> Linux evdev keycode, plus pynput key-name
// fallback, for the RemoteDesk web client.
//
// GENERATED by gen_keymap.py from Chromium ui/events/keycodes/dom/dom_code_data.inc
// (refs/heads/main fetched 2026-10-19, sha256 841e2c58e6388f14736717eb6e365c8b8e9767788e36339bf1d35a37ab48e5b2).
// Every row there satisfies XKB = evdev + 8, i.e. the same convention the desktop
// viewer uses on X11 (remotedesk/keymap.py: x11_keycode_to_evdev = native - 8).
//
// Wire format (remotedesk/protocol.py):  {t: "key", down, sc, k}
//   sc: evdev code (0 if unknown)   k: pynput Key name or single character (fallback)
// The host injects `sc` when it can (XTEST on X11; SendInput scancode on Windows for
// evdev 1..0x53, 0x56..0x58 and the extended keys in keymap.py) and falls back to `k`.

